Fix                                                                             

Increase the memory limit for the frontend-proxy deployment to a value that     
comfortably fits its runtime needs (e.g., 256Mi or higher) and redeploy:        

                                                                                
 # Patch example (apply with kubectl)                                           
 kubectl -n astronomy-shop set resources deployment/frontend-proxy \            
   --limits=memory=256Mi \                                                      
   --requests=memory=128Mi                                                      
                                                                                

After applying the new limits, the pod should start without OOM kills, the      
CrashLoopBackOff will resolve, and the frontend will be able to route traffic to
the microservices, restoring normal operation of the OpenTelemetry Demo         
Astronomy Shop.                                                                 

